  "notes": "Third-party BatteryLife v12 copy of the Sandia (SNL) cycling data: the original BatteryArchive CSV files are not in Raw_Dataset. Each pickle carries its own materials, nominal capacity and voltage limits; the test conditions are encoded in the cell id. The delivered 61 cells span LFP (18), NCA (22) and NMC (21), with nominal Ah values 1.1 (18 cells), 2.88 (4), 3.2 (18), 2.7 (4), and 3.0 (17). The collection-level 1.1 Ah is a modal representative, not a shared capacity; use per-cell specifications. Delivered lower cutoffs are 2.0/2.5 V and upper cutoffs 3.6/4.2 V. The independent scan found 10,992,431 finite temperature values among 11,572,303 entries; presence does not imply complete coverage. Charging profile: the charge is the same 0.5C everywhere; the discharge C-rate differs between cells. 4 NCA cells (20-80% SOC window) charge at constant current only. Cell makers and models per chemistry are from the SNL cycling paper (Preger et al. 2020, full text read): LFP A123 APR18650M1A (1.1 Ah), NCA Panasonic NCR18650B (3.2 Ah), NMC LG Chem 18650HG2 (3 Ah). The paper's capacities do not include the 2.88 Ah (NCA) and 2.7 Ah (NMC) values some pickles carry; those are kept as recorded and listed in the discrepancy matrix. The primary source of the SNL cells is Preger et al., J. Electrochem. Soc. 2020 (10.1149/1945-7111/abae37); the delivered copy is the BatteryLife release (Tan et al., KDD 2025, 10.1145/3711896.3737372). The full text of Preger et al. (J. Electrochem. Soc. 167 (2020) 120532) confirms: A123 APR18650M1A LFP (1.1 Ah, 3.3 V, 2-3.6 V), Panasonic NCR18650B NCA (3.2 Ah, 3.6 V, 2.5-4.2 V) and LG Chem 18650HG2 NMC (3 Ah, 3.6 V, 2-4.2 V), all 18650; cathodes by ICP-OES NMC Ni0.84Mn0.06Co0.1 and NCA likely Ni0.81Co0.14Al0.05; test matrix of Table II (DOD 40-60, 20-80 and 0-100% at 25 C and 0.5C, 1C, 2C, 3C discharge, plus 0-100% at 15 and 35 C at 1C and 2C), every condition on at least two cells, a nearly three-year study on Arbin testers (SCTS and LBT21084) in Tenney T10C-1.5 chambers with a K- or T-type thermocouple taped to each cell skin, round of 125 to 1000 cycles (halved after more than 5% loss). C-rates use the nominal capacities above. The paper's nominal capacities do not include the 2.88 Ah (NCA) and 2.7 Ah (NMC) pickle values, which stay listed in the discrepancy matrix. Of the 18 LFP cells the pickles carry 1.1 Ah, matching Table I; the pickles' 61 cells exceed the paper's two cells per condition because the BatteryLife release adds more tests. Rate combinations: the 0-100% SOC cells charge CC-CV at 0.5C and discharge at 0.5, 1, 2 or 3C; the four NCA cells of the 20-80% window charge CC only at 0.5C and discharge at 0.5C (per-cell attributes)."
